FIX (medium): Chatbot SSE whitespace loss. In /app/backend/server.py change `yield f"data: {token}

"` to `yield f"data:{token}

"` (no space after the colon) OR base64/JSON-encode the token. The frontend Chatbot.jsx consumer also needs to honour the change. Alternatively render markdown in the panel and replace newlines properly.

rca of the issue:
Chatbot whitespace loss RCA: SSE spec (W3C) strips at most one leading U+0020 SPACE character from each `data:` line during parsing. Server emits `data: {token}

`. When Claude streams a chunk like ` for`, the on-the-wire line is `data:  for` and parsers reconstruct it as ` for` (one space lost). Subsequent token concatenation produces 'demandsfor'. Fix: drop the space after `data:` on the server, or wrap each token in JSON e.g. `data:{"t":"..."}

` and parse on client. Reproduction: open chatbot, click 'What is Performance Ayurveda?' — observe missing word boundaries in the response.
